== @GNG:lo <sec:algos_gng>
Our supervisor kickstarted the exploration by suggesting @GNG networks 
@growing_neural_gas when the initial goal was being established.
Even after exploring various implementations, we concluded that @GNG was 
not particularly relevant for growing trees, nor was it effective for 
real-time even with major optimizations @growing_neural_gas_efficient.

=== Good Spacing <sec:algos_gng_spacing>
Possible uses we came up with were related to creating bounding geometry for 
tree crowns by training it on natural shapes and existing trees. 
Constructing meshes for rendering was also an idea, but grew out of scope.

On the subject of @GNG, we also got to explore the @LOD aspect and found 
interesting applications for compressing point cloud colors 
@neural_gas_color_object_reconstruct, but without advance in _growing_ trees.
